<!--
  Hardened Runtime entitlements for the bundled bt_attach ERTS release
  (ADR 0097, BT-2987). Applied to every nested Mach-O binary under
  dist-liveview/ (beam.smp, epmd, NIF .so/.dylib files) by
  scripts/ci/sign-macos-nested-binaries.sh BEFORE `cargo tauri build` copies
  them into the app bundle, and to the top-level app itself via this file's
  path in tauri.conf.json's `bundle.macOS.entitlements`.

  Without these, the Hardened Runtime that macOS notarization requires
  blocks the BEAM VM outright: BeamAsm (OTP's JIT, default since OTP 24)
  needs allow-jit + allow-unsigned-executable-memory to allocate executable
  memory at runtime, and NIFs load as independently-built, independently-
  (or un-)signed dynamic libraries that library validation would otherwise
  refuse to load. This is the general Hardened-Runtime shape any BEAM-
  bundling desktop app needs (see ADR 0097 Prior Art re: Livebook) — not
  yet confirmed against a real `cargo tauri build` in this sandbox (no
  macOS/Tauri toolchain available; see desktop/README.md).

  Deliberate over-grant, flagged in review: this same set is applied to
  EVERY signed binary (beam.smp, but also epmd/run_erl/to_erl/and other
  small ERTS helpers that never touch JIT-allocated memory or load NIFs).
  Only beam.smp strictly needs allow-jit/allow-unsigned-executable-memory;
  only beam.smp (and anything hosting NIFs) needs disable-library-
  validation. A narrower per-binary entitlement set is more correct but
  requires knowing exactly which ERTS helper binaries exist and what each
  does across OTP versions — the single-set approach here trades that
  precision for simplicity, matching the approach the ADR's own prior-art
  comparison (Livebook) takes. The entitlements do not expand the app's
  OS-level sandbox regardless, so the practical exposure is limited; if a
  future review wants the narrower version, it needs a real macOS build to
  verify each helper binary still works signed with a reduced set.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
